  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Liquified Natural Gas Receiving Terminal and Distribution Network in Bok Region, through Plum Energy LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant partially funds a feasibility study to assess the economic, financial, and technical viability of a liquified natural gas (LNG) receiving terminal and distribution network near the Port of Kamsar in the Bok region of Guinea (Project). The Project is expected to help diversify Guinea&apos;s energy market that currently depends on hydropower, diesel, and heavy fuel oil. The Project is expected to build a large-scale LNG receiving terminal, storage tanks, high-capacity regasification units, and distribution infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
